WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.088
<v Examiner>Four marks.

2
00:00:02.088 --> 00:00:04.490
<v Examiner>Compare burnout and compassion fatigue,

3
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.557
<v Examiner>and describe self-care strategies that build a nurse's resilience.

4
00:00:09.007 --> 00:00:12.100
Compare means define both, then say how they relate.

5
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:16.727
Burnout is an occupational phenomenon, not a medical condition.

6
00:00:16.727 --> 00:00:21.965
It comes from long-term, unmanaged workplace stress, and it has three features:

7
00:00:21.965 --> 00:00:27.866
exhaustion, mental distance or cynicism about the job, and reduced professional efficacy.

8
00:00:27.866 --> 00:00:30.783
A nurse with burnout still feels compassion.

9
00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:35.955
It builds up over time, it's caused by a stressful, negative work environment,

10
00:00:35.955 --> 00:00:39.204
and it may not affect relationships outside work.

11
00:00:39.654 --> 00:00:44.796
Compassion fatigue comes from the emotional demands of caring for people who are

12
00:00:44.796 --> 00:00:48.460
suffering: absorbing their suffering as secondary trauma.

13
00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:53.859
It leads to physical, psychological and spiritual exhaustion, and a loss of empathy.

14
00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:58.937
Its symptoms include irritability, anger, depression and less pleasure in life.

15
00:00:58.937 --> 00:01:03.115
It can happen right after one traumatic experience, or over time,

16
00:01:03.115 --> 00:01:06.521
and it can interfere with relationships outside work.

17
00:01:06.971 --> 00:01:10.786
So the key difference: burnout comes from the work environment,

18
00:01:10.786 --> 00:01:12.421
and compassion survives it.

19
00:01:12.421 --> 00:01:17.083
Compassion fatigue comes from caring itself, and compassion is what it takes.

20
00:01:17.533 --> 00:01:22.995
Self-care is deliberate action to look after every part of your health and wellbeing.

21
00:01:22.995 --> 00:01:28.135
It's enjoyable, it re-energises you, it is not selfish, and it needs boundaries.

22
00:01:28.135 --> 00:01:30.127
Numbing activities don't count.

23
00:01:30.127 --> 00:01:34.625
Strategies from the deck: set realistic goals, let go of some control,

24
00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:39.315
change negative thinking, communicate, use humour, plus regular exercise,

25
00:01:39.315 --> 00:01:42.078
journalling and seven to nine hours' sleep.

26
00:01:42.078 --> 00:01:43.877
Self-care builds resilience:

27
00:01:43.877 --> 00:01:47.861
the ability to adapt positively to stress and recover quickly,

28
00:01:47.861 --> 00:01:52.102
which protects nurses against both burnout and compassion fatigue.

29
00:01:52.552 --> 00:01:58.007
Burnout: from long-term workplace stress; exhaustion, cynicism, reduced efficacy;

30
00:01:58.007 --> 00:02:00.566
compassion survives; builds over time.

31
00:02:00.566 --> 00:02:05.616
Compassion fatigue: from absorbing patients' suffering as secondary trauma;

32
00:02:05.616 --> 00:02:08.175
loss of empathy; can follow one event.

33
00:02:08.175 --> 00:02:12.620
Self-care is deliberate, enjoyable, not selfish, needs boundaries;

34
00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.909
it builds resilience against both.
